</section>

<section class="section section-subtle">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <h2 class="section-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Can I try Exceptionless before I buy? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Yes. Sign up with no credit card and send your first events on the Free plan. When you're ready for real-time alerts, integrations, longer retention, more users, or Exie, upgrade in a couple of clicks.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I change or cancel my plan at any time? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Yes. Upgrade, downgrade, or switch between monthly and yearly billing from your organization's billing page. If you no longer want to use Exceptionless, cancel before your next billing period.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What counts as an event? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Every error, log message, feature usage, 404, or custom event your apps send counts as one event. Session heartbeats don't count toward your limit, and you can use client configuration and log levels to control how much you send.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens if I go over my event limit? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Exceptionless stops accepting new events until your next billing period and lets you know, so you can upgrade if you need more room. You're never charged surprise overage fees, and the data you've already collected isn't affected.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What are premium features? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          Premium features are included on every paid plan:
          <ul>
            <li>Advanced search and filtering on any field</li>
            <li>Real-time notifications for new, regressed, and critical errors (the free plan gets daily summaries)</li>
            <li>Slack, webhook, and Zapier integrations</li>
            <li>Geolocation of events</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which plans include Exie? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">The Exie AI assistant is included with Medium, Large, Extra Large, and Enterprise plans. Each plan includes a monthly AI usage allowance, and there's nothing extra to set up.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which plans include the MCP server? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">All of them, including Free. The MCP server lets coding agents like Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot, and OpenCode work with your errors, and it uses your plan like any other API access, with no extra charge. <a href="/docs/ai/mcp-server/">Set up the MCP server</a>.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How much do I save with yearly billing? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Yearly plans are priced at 11 months, so you get one month free compared to paying monthly.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I host Exceptionless myself? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Absolutely. Exceptionless is open source under the Apache 2.0 license and you can run it on your own infrastructure with Docker or Kubernetes. You take on operating Elasticsearch, storage, backups, and upgrades, which the hosted service handles for you. See the <a href="/docs/self-hosting/">self-hosting guide</a> to get started, or browse the code on <a href="{{ site.githubUrl }}">GitHub</a>.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Need something else? {{ icons["chevron-down"] }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">If you need more events, longer retention, or have questions about billing, <a href="/contact/">send us a message</a> or reach us through <strong>Help &rarr; Support</strong> in the app.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta reveal">
      <h2>Get set up in minutes</h2>
      <p>No credit card required to sign up. Upgrade when you're ready for real-time alerts, integrations, and Exie.</p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="{{ site.signupUrl }}" data-cta="pricing-footer">Get started {{ icons["arrow-right"] }}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg" href="/contact/">Talk to us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
